# Elegy Acolyte (4/4 lifelink). Turn 1: Dark Ritual (an instant, which leaves the stack, not the battlefield) and two
# Moxen pay for it; nothing nonland leaves the battlefield and no spell is warped, so the Void ability finds its
# "if" false at the beginning of Bot1's end step and no Robot appears (checked at Bot2's turn). Turn 3: the Acolyte
# is unblocked and deals 4 combat damage to Bot2: lifelink gains 4 and "whenever one or more creatures you control
# deal combat damage to a player" draws one card and loses 1 life: 20 + 4 - 1 = 23, Bot2 at 16. Hand: three Islands
# left on turn 1, one drawn for the turn, one drawn by the trigger = 5.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dark Ritual
Mox Ruby
Elegy Acolyte
Island x3
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dark Ritual.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elegy Acolyte.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Elegy Acolyte
? Bot1.Life = 20
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Elegy Acolyte > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Life = 23
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Elegy Acolyte
